B.aEy=new A.hQ()
B.Wu=new A.dL("inspect-washer-drain-filter","Look at the drain filter or coin trap","Unplug the washer (or switch off its breaker) before opening a filter cover. Do not split a sealed tub or pump. Place a pan only after this look if you later open the access.","At the lower front corner of the cabinet, find the small square access door or twist-off knob for the coin trap / drain filter. From outside, look whether lint or coins are packed in that opening. Do not unscrew a sealed pump.","You can see the typical access, and from outside it is not stuffed with lint, coins, or sludge.","The trap looks packed with lint, coins, or sludge, or the cover cannot seat. Still do not split a sealed pump.","washer","washer-drain-filter-access",B.dD,B.x7,"washer-drain-filter-access")
B.iH=s(["washer-drain-hose-not-seated"],t.s)
B.aEz=new A.hQ()
B.WD=new A.dL("inspect-washer-standpipe","Look at the drain hose in the standpipe","Unplug the washer before pulling it out or reaching behind it. Do not split a sealed tub or pump. No live electrical testing.","Behind the washer, find the drain hose end. It should sit inside the vertical standpipe (or hooked over a laundry tub) with a clip or hook holding it so it cannot slip out onto the floor.","The hose is seated in the standpipe (or tub) and looks clipped or hooked so it cannot drop out.","The hose is hanging free, barely hooked, or water would pour on the floor instead of into the pipe \u2014 a common after-move or new-install miss.","washer","washer-standpipe-hose",B.dD,B.iH,"washer-standpipe-hose")
B.a0i=s(["washer-drain-hose-not-seated","kinked-or-clogged-washer-drain-hose"],t.s)
B.WH=new A.dL("inspect-washer-drain-hose-config","Look at how the drain hose is run","Unplug before pulling the washer out. This is a look-only check. Do not cut plumbing or open a sealed pump. No live electrical testing.","Follow the drain hose from the washer cabinet to the standpipe. Check that it is connected at both ends, stays round (not crushed), has no sharp kink, and that only a short length sits in the pipe \u2014 not stuffed deep.","The hose is connected, not crushed, and only a short length sits in the standpipe \u2014 not jammed down the pipe.","It is disconnected, flattened, sharply bent, or stuffed deep into the standpipe (a common incorrect setup).","washer","washer-drain-hose-look",B.dD,B.a0i,"washer-drain-hose-look")
B.wT=s(["closed-taps-or-kinked-inlet","clogged-washer-inlet-screens"],t.s)
B.WA=new A.dL("inspect-washer-taps-inlet","Look at the taps and inlet hose","This is a look at the taps and the visible hose. Do not open the cabinet, inlet valve body, or any wiring. No live electrical testing.","At the wall behind the washer, both hot and cold taps should be fully open (handles in line with the pipe). The inlet hose should be round, not sharply kinked or crushed.","Both taps look fully open and the visible inlet hose is not kinked.","A tap is closed or only partly open, or the inlet hose is kinked or crushed.","washer","washer-taps-open",B.j2,B.wT,"washer-taps-open")
B.iG=s(["clogged-washer-inlet-screens"],t.s)
B.WB=new A.dL("inspect-washer-inlet-screens","Look at the inlet-hose screens","Unplug the washer and close both taps before loosening a coupling. Stay at the hose ends. Do not open the inlet valve body or cabinet wiring. No live electrical testing.","At the tap end of each inlet hose, look at the small screen or washer in the coupling. Packed grit or scale can starve fill even when taps are open.","The small screens at the hose ends look clear \u2014 not packed with grit.","A screen looks packed with grit or scale. Still do not open the valve body.","washer","washer-inlet-screens-look",B.dD,B.iG,"washer-inlet-screens-look")
B.aeq=new A.w(B.dG,["Not leaking","Yes","Not sure","Already checked"],t.w)
