s($,"byq","bbx",()=>{var q=u.B,p="Clear the lint and vent path",o="Clean the lint filter and clear crush, kinks, or packed lint from the vent path you can reach safely.",n="This corrects the overheating cause. On a fuse or high-limit path it does not restore heat by itself.",m="Unplug before moving the dryer. Do not dismantle vent runs inside walls."
return A.ac(["qualified technician",A.hs("Book professional service rather than continuing. Describe the symptoms and the safe checks you already completed.","A technician needs meter readings or cabinet work. That is outside beginner steps.","Hand off to a qualified technician","Do not continue past this point yourself, and do not run the dryer again if it overheated."),"thermal fuse",A.hs("Unplug and turn off the breaker. Open the heater service panel (front lower or rear on many models \u2014 check your manual). Swap the fuse for an exact-match part. Never jumper or test it live.","A one-shot fuse opened because the dryer overheated. Replacing it without fixing restricted airflow can open again.","Replace the thermal fuse with power fully off","Do not meter live circuits or bypass the fuse. Stop for smoke or burning smell."),"exact-match part",A.hs("Match the part number or take the old fuse to a parts counter. Install only with power fully isolated.","Wrong parts or bypassing protection can cause fire risk or repeat failure.","Use the correct replacement fuse for your model","Do not substitute foil or wire. Stop for smoke or burning smell."),"heater service panel",A.hs("With power off, remove the front lower panel or rear panel per your model label or manual \u2014 screw locations vary by brand.","Access exposes the heater housing and fuse but still requires power to stay off.","Open the correct service panel for heater access","Do not open panels with power on. Stop for smoke or burning smell."),"high-limit",A.hs("Leave the high-limit thermostat in place. Correct the airflow cause and let a technician service the protection itself.","High-limit protection is the last defence against an overheating dryer.","Never bypass high-limit protection","Thermostat replacement and heater-housing work are technician tasks."),"set to heat",A.hs("Look at the control panel and make sure the cycle is not Air Fluff, Air Dry, or another no-heat setting.","Air-only settings tumble without heat, which looks exactly like a heating fault.","Confirm a heat cycle is selected",q),"short heat cycle",A.hs("Restore power, start a few minutes on a heat cycle with the drum turning, then carefully feel whether the load is warm.","Warmth returning points to the airflow path. Still completely cold points to an interrupted heater circuit.","Run a short heat test cycle","Stop the cycle immediately for smoke, a burning smell, or sparking."),"vent path",A.hs(o,n,p,m),"vent restrictions",A.hs(o,n,p,m),"vent hose",A.hs("Check airflow before opening the cabinet. Unplug if you need to roll the dryer. Check the visible hose only.",u.fV,"Check the visible vent hose","Unplug before moving the dryer. Do not puncture or dismantle hidden vent runs."),"lint filter",A.hs("Check airflow before opening the cabinet. Pull out only the removable screen. Do not open panels for this check.","Better airflow after cleaning supports a lint-restriction cause.","Check the lint filter",q),"unplug",A.hs("Unplug the dryer from the wall or switch off its dedicated breaker before moving it or opening access panels.","Power is off so you can inspect safely without live parts.","Disconnect power before touching the dryer","Never work on a plugged-in dryer beyond normal button use."),"do not measure live",A.hs("Use only external observations \u2014 settings, sounds, warmth, and plug condition. Do not probe terminals or heaters with tools.","You avoid high-voltage shock risk while still gathering useful clues.","No live electrical testing","If the problem requires meter readings or wiring checks, call a professional."),"vent hood",A.hs("Check airflow before opening the cabinet. Stay outside. Feel or listen for air and whether the flap opens.","A free-opening hood with strong airflow supports good exhaust.","Check the outside vent hood","Do not enter unsafe roof or crawl areas."),"gas ignition",A.hs("External gas supply valve and cycle checks only. Do not disassemble gas lines, burners, igniters, or valves.","Gas ignition faults require a qualified gas technician.","No DIY gas ignition repair","If gas odor is present, stop use, ventilate, and follow gas emergency procedures."),"gas technician",A.hs("Do not attempt gas valve, igniter, burner, or flame-sensor repair. Schedule professional gas appliance service.","Gas heat restoration is not a beginner DIY task.","Call a qualified gas technician","Any gas odor \u2014 stop use, ventilate, evacuate if needed, follow gas emergency procedures."),"capacitor",A.hs("Listen for hum/struggle at Start only. Do not open the motor compartment or test capacitors.","Start assist faults require professional motor service.","No live motor or capacitor work","Stop for burning smell, smoke, or repeated failed start attempts.")],t.N,A.ag("bX"))})
